Battery state of the Google Pixel 7

The component 'max77759_battery' reads the fuel gauge of the MAX77759 through
an I2c session every 'period_ms' and writes the report 'battery':

! battery | percent: 87 | voltage_mv: 4212 | current_ma: -312
!         | charging: no | temp_c: 29

'current_ma' is positive while current flows into the battery. After three
failed periods in a row the last values get 'stale: yes'.

The component never writes a register of the gauge, every access is a write
of the register pointer and a two-byte read. The same bus carries the charger
and the over-voltage protection, so the policy of 'gs201_i2c' should limit
the session to the gauge with 'max_write: 1':

! + allow  | bus_address: 0x36
! + policy | label_prefix: battery | bus_address: 0x36 | max_write: 1

Config, with the defaults:

! config | period_ms: 5000 | rsense_uohm: 5000

:period_ms:   period of the readings, at least 100.
:rsense_uohm: sense resistor of the gauge, 5 mOhm on the Pixel 7.

The register meanings and the rules of the monitor have no Genode
dependencies ('gauge.h') and host tests:

! make -C repos/pixel/src/driver/battery/max77759/test

The scenario 'run/battery_pixel' logs the readings every two seconds:

! make run/battery_pixel KERNEL=hw BOARD=google_pixel7
